guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/jon-ossoff-wins-georgia-senate-election-midterms-mike-collins-rcna603336</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/jon-ossoff-wins-georgia-senate-election-midterms-mike-collins-rcna603336</link><media:content url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261021-jon-ossoff-georgia-senate-midterms-vsb-2205-2fdffd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1667" width="2500"><media:credit>Elijah Nouvelage</media:credit><media:text type="plain">U.S. Senator Jon Ossoff.</media:text><media:description type="plain">Sen. Jon Ossoff during a campaign event in Marietta, Ga., in October.</media:description></media:content><media:content url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261021-mike-collins-georgia-senator-midterms-vsb-2216-9f617b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1666" width="2500"><media:credit>Kevin Dietsch</media:credit><media:text type="plain">U.S. Rep. Mike Collins.</media:text><media:description type="plain">Sen. Jon Ossoff during a campaign event in Marietta, Ga., in October.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261021-jon-ossoff-georgia-senate-midterms-vsb-2205-2fdffd.jpg" height="1667" width="2500"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:31:05 GMT</pubDate><title>Democratic Sen. Jon Ossoff cruises to re-election in Georgia</title><updateDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:31:05 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Scott Wong</dc:creator><dc:contributor>Ben Kamisar</dc:contributor><dateTimeWritten>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:45:40 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>A handful of House Republican incumbents were caught up in tough races in districts President Donald Trump carried in 2024 — an encouraging sign for Democrats as they fight to retake the majority from the GOP.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/democrats-republicans-battle-for-house-trump-washington-midterm-rcna605760</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/democrats-republicans-battle-for-house-trump-washington-midterm-rcna605760</link><media:content url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261030-congress-results-mainbar-jg-3462a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1600" width="2400"><media:credit>Justine Goode</media:credit><media:text type="plain"></media:text><media:description type="plain"></media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261030-congress-results-mainbar-jg-3462a8.jpg" height="1600" width="2400"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:45:40 GMT</pubDate><title>Democrats have polling and history on their side in House races</title><updateDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:46:22 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Henry J. Gomez</dc:creator><dc:contributor>Ben Kamisar</dc:contributor><dateTimeWritten>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:45:40 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Control of the Senate is on the line Tuesday following a midterm election cycle with races marked by betrayal and alleged ballot shenanigans.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/republicans-fight-hold-senate-democrats-rcna605762</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/republicans-fight-hold-senate-democrats-rcna605762</link><media:content url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261030-senate-results-mainbar-jg-99b601.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1600" width="2400"><media:credit>Justine Goode</media:credit><media:text type="plain"></media:text><media:description type="plain"></media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261030-senate-results-mainbar-jg-99b601.jpg" height="1600" width="2400"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:45:40 GMT</pubDate><title>GOP fights to hang on to Senate majority</title><updateDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:42:15 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>John Lapinski</dc:creator><dc:creator>Stephen Pettigrew</dc:creator><dc:creator>Marc Trussler</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:15:09 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Americans might be waiting awhile. It all depends on how states count their votes and how close the races will be.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/decision-desk-will-know-senate-house-control-rcna603038</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/decision-desk-will-know-senate-house-control-rcna603038</link><media:content url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261012-jeffries-johnson-gavel-sjr-1456-133e88.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1454" width="2180"><media:credit>Chip Somodevilla</media:credit><media:text type="plain">U.S. House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries passes the gavel to Speaker of the House Mike Johnson.</media:text><media:description type="plain">What has to happen for Republicans to keep their narrow majority, and what would cause a narrow Democratic win?</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261012-jeffries-johnson-gavel-sjr-1456-133e88.jpg" height="1454" width="2180"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:15:09 GMT</pubDate><title>Inside the Decision Desk: When will we know Senate and House control?</title><updateDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:15:09 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Stephanie Perry, NBC News Exit Poll Desk </dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 10:00:40 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Before votes are tallied on election night, exit polls offer an early look at who is voting and what is motivating their choices.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/nbc-news-exit-poll-how-works-results-election-night-rcna606180</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/nbc-news-exit-poll-how-works-results-election-night-rcna606180</link><media:content url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261028-maine-polling-station-ch-1618-28ea65.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1667" width="2500"><media:credit>Li Rui</media:credit><media:text type="plain">A person casts their vote.</media:text><media:description type="plain">A man fills out his ballot at a polling station in Bangor, Maine, on Oct. 16, 2026.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url="https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261028-maine-polling-station-ch-1618-28ea65.jpg" height="1667" width="2500"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 10:00:40 GMT</pubDate><title>NBC News Exit Poll: How it works and how we use the results on election night</title><updateDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 10:00:40 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dateTimeWritten>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:43:23 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>NBC News projects that Democratic Sen. Jon Ossoff will win re-election in Georgia. NBC News&#39; Steve Kornacki breaks down how the Democrat performed in counties in the state.</description><expires>2056-11-03T23:42:26.000+0000</expires><guid isPermaLink="false">nbc_spec_ossoff_wins_georgia_261103</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/video/democratic-sen-jon-ossoff-projected-to-win-re-election-in-georgia-272808517979</link><media:content url="https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbc_spec_ossoff_wins_georgia_261103/1/abs/index.m3u8" medium="video"><media:credit></media:credit><media:title>Democratic Sen. 